  "body": {
    "title": "Unify terminal bootstrap verification and runtime handoff",
    "summary": "Adapt both shared terminal templates, renderer and publication helper to the same verified external store. Authenticate cached/fresh Node and control bytes before execution, publish under the existing lock, wait for exact helper exit, then invoke the canonical runtime manager with fresh ordinary admission.",
    "size": "M",
    "order": 5,
    "acceptanceChecks": [
      "Manual and IDE-generated POSIX/PowerShell scripts use fixed independent Node/control digests and need no host Node; matching verified cached runtime/control can work offline while missing prerequisites fail clearly.",
      "The exact publication-helper child exits before the final manager starts/acquires a fresh lock; no inherited lock/session/source flag, PID heuristic or successful install claim substitutes for admission.",
      "Paths with spaces/Unicode/apostrophes, interruption, concurrent bootstrap and Windows nonmoving execution-stage behavior are covered by surrounding fixtures.",
      "Terminal owns prompts/I/O and existing same-terminal TUI semantics; no IDE adapter redesign or current host daemon operation is performed."
    ],
    "tests": [
      {
        "level": "integration",
        "name": "bootstrap-no-host-node-verifies-archive-and-executable-before-execution"
      },
      {
        "level": "integration",
        "name": "bootstrap-native-operation-lock-exclusive-publication-exact-helper-exit-then-fresh-manager-lock"
      },
      {
        "level": "integration",
        "name": "bootstrap-publication-stage-distinct-from-running-node-and-loaded-native-library"
      },
      {
        "level": "integration",
        "name": "runtime-stage-cancellation-conflict-and-uncertain-closure-retain-safe-state"
      },
      {
        "level": "integration",
        "name": "bootstrap-verified-cached-runtime-control-offline-with-host-node-trap-and-quoted-paths"
      }
    ],
